    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></math> denote the complement of an event <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> be any pairwise independent events with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8745;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8745;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>&#8745;</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
  },
